# San Carlos permit-intel (sca-permits) environment.
#
# Public search + detail on the Tyler EnerGov CSS portal are ANONYMOUS — verified
# 2026-05-26 the search API returns 200 with NO Authorization header. So normally
# you need NOTHING here to run step 0/1.
#
# Fallback only: if the portal ever starts rejecting anonymous requests (401/403),
# paste a Bearer token from a logged-in browser session here for the run. The
# scraper performs NO login itself; you authenticate, we reuse the session token.
SCA_BEARER_TOKEN=

# Cloudflare D1 (step 4 — `python3 src/step4_sync_d1.py --execute`).
# Decided: publish into the SHARED `permits` D1 (the sca_ table prefix keeps the
# tables clear of the other cities'), so the frontend reads all cities from one
# DB. Point CF_D1_DATABASE_ID at the EXISTING `permits` database id, not a new one.
# Only needed for --execute; without these, step 4 just generates SQL locally.
# CF_ACCOUNT_ID=
# CF_D1_DATABASE_ID=        # the shared `permits` D1 id
# CF_API_TOKEN=

# NOTE: NO proxy. San Carlos is a public JSON API on tylerhost.net with no
# Cloudflare gate; a polite single-IP direct scrape is correct. Do NOT set a proxy.
